4. Research the difference between SSD and HDD storage, then write a short comparison (3 points) explaining which one is better for a student who wants fast boot times and why.
=>Speed – SSDs are 5–10× faster than HDDs at reading and writing data. A computer with an SSD typically boots in 10–20 seconds; an HDD often takes 40–90+ seconds.
Reliability & Noise – SSDs have no moving parts, so they are quieter, more shock-resistant, and less likely to fail from physical impact (important for a laptop a student carries around).
Which is better? – SSD is clearly better for a student who wants fast boot times. The speed difference is dramatic and immediately noticeable every time you turn on the computer or open programs. The only remaining advantage of HDDs is lower cost per gigabyte for pure bulk storage, but for the main system drive, an SSD is the superior choice.
